## THE DONE RULE (C-79; quote it from the file, at write time, exactly)
The product owner's words, `CLARIFICATIONS.md:1714`: *"Done means merged to main, the same as Composer"*. **The test, `CLARIFICATIONS.md:1716` (C-79 `Settles:`), recorded there as the coordinator's reading, not the product owner's words:** "a ticket moves to Done when its change is merged to main AND each Done-when clause of the ticket is MET; a clause that needs a deploy, a words approval or a further ruling is still not met by a merge ...; a merge alone never moves a ticket; the rule is silent on tickets whose work is done by a ruling or a measurement with no merged change ..., which stay as they are." **Verified at drafting: root main `b35d925e` holds this text at lines 1714 and 1716 (`/usr/bin/grep -n -i`; control: the heading at 1712).** The three conditions for a move (`CLARIFICATIONS.md:1727`, B1004 item 1), all required: (1) slot `DONE-SLOT` reads `MOVE-TO-DONE`; (2) your Done-when table (Step 4a) reads MET for every clause; (3) no gate or review line and no red run contradicts it. The readings you may use, each only as worded where it stands: (a) to (d) at `:1727`; (e) to (h) at `:1782` (B1019 item 1); (i) in B1021's item 1 (section at `:1835`, item 1 at `:1839`; slot `CAP-READING` is not given in this kit: none of the 21 keys has a cap NO GO as its last gate, re-check at 4a, and a cap NO GO found there is comment-only); (j) to (n) in B1064's item 1 (`:1957`): (k) a residual held only as a backlog row holds the ticket where the stamp says so, (l) a behavioural clause no gate ran is read from the source and the record says it is a read, (m) a clause whose worded means cannot produce the state it names is met by a different means where the gate measured the property. In Jira text the rule is cited as "the product owner's 2026-11-01 ruling that Done means merged to main", never by a card id.
**A ruling or default behind a key (the drafter read the lines; you re-read them at Step 1 and quote the ruling at its source in the comment where it bears):** MPSCALC-194 (`CLARIFICATIONS.md` C-37, the sentence for a feedback-only 401, the product owner's 2026-10-17 ruling; the unsent-text half "is not in this ruling and stays open", comments 39568, 39594, 39642), MPSCALC-203 (C-39, retention: keep the copy only when the deploy stops, delete it after a clean check; "the rest of this ticket's acceptance" is open, comments 39567, 39596, 39644), MPSCALC-247 to -251 (C-45, the v13 build plan, D-10 and D-13), MPSCALC-93 and -100 (C-24, the empty and whitespace-only author, a coordinator ruling recorded as a ruling and not as a C-entry; read the lines). Find each heading by case-insensitive regex.

